<h2>Two orders that are constantly confused</h2>
<div class="compare">
  <div class="col old"><strong>Suspension of sentence + bail</strong><p>Standard relief pending appeal. The appellant remains a convict for every legal purpose; only the execution of the punishment is deferred. Disqualifications and service consequences continue to operate.</p></div>
  <div class="arrow">→</div>
  <div class="col new"><strong>Stay of conviction</strong><p>Exceptional relief. The finding of guilt itself is placed in abeyance for identified purposes, arresting the collateral consequences — but only where the court is shown precisely what irreversible damage the conviction is causing.</p></div>
